<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoàn Kiếm Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Hoan Kiem Lake, Lake of the Returned Sword</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hoàn Kiếm Lake, the 'Lake of the Returned Sword', is a lake in the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. According to legend, after defeating the Ming, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Lê Lợi</a> returned his magic sword to a golden turtle that rose from the lake. On its small islands stand the Turtle Tower and the Temple of the Jade Mountain, and the lake is a symbol of the city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hoan-kiem-lake.jpg" alt="Hoàn Kiếm Lake" width="320" height="275" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cyril Doussin from London, United Kingdom · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thap_Rua.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
